{
  "description": "Golden vocabulary import/export vectors (issue #2409). Every head's CSV and TXT writer must produce `csv` / `txt` byte for byte from `entries`, and every head's reader must turn `csv` and `txt` back into `entries` (the round trip). `csvImport` / `txtImport` hold files written by hand or by another app: `expected` is the parsed rows in file order, before the merge into the store, and `skipped` counts words dropped for being longer than 1000 characters (VocabularyWords.MaxWordChars, #2390). A null replacement means none. Rules: CSV is UTF-8 RFC 4180, header `word,replacement`, CRLF rows, a field quoted only when it holds a comma, a double quote, CR or LF; the reader accepts a BOM, LF or CRLF, no header, one column, extra columns (ignored) and blank rows (ignored); the header is the first row when its first field is `word` (any case). TXT is UTF-8, LF rows, one term per line, a replacement after the first tab; in the replacement a backslash is written `\\\\` and a line break `\\n` (other backslashes read as themselves); a tab inside a word is written as a space. Both readers trim words and replacements, treat a blank replacement as none, split a word that spans lines into one word per line with the same replacement (#1777), and skip blank words.",
